<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`pairLInsert` commutative).** Insertion of left children in the topped domain commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens and commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`pairRInsert` commutative).** Insertion of right children in the topped domain commutes.

*Proof.* By cases on the two tokens and commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`IsUToken` decidable).** Whether a topped token belongs to the universal domain is decidable.

*Proof.* By cases on the token, excluding the top. □

**Definition (`UToken` equality).** Equality of universal tokens is decidable.

*Proof.* It is equality of the underlying topped tokens. □

**Definition (`uForgetInsert` commutative).** Forgetting the top commutes with insertion.

*Proof.* By commutativity of finite-set insertion. □

**Definition (`VToken`).** A token of the topped domain is bottom, top, or a left or right child.


**Definition (`pairLInsert`).** The left-child insertion adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


**Definition (`vPairLFinset`).** The v Pair Lfinite set.


**Theorem (`mem_foldr_pairL`).** A token lies in the fold of left children exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_vPairLFinset`).** A token lies in the mem v Pair Lfinite set exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`vPairLFinset.insert_top`).** Inserting the indicated constructor updates insert top by adding that payload.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`pairRInsert`).** The right-child insertion adds the payload of the matching constructor and leaves every other constructor unchanged.


**Definition (`vPairRFinset`).** The v Pair Rfinite set.


**Theorem (`mem_foldr_pairR`).** A token lies in the fold of right children exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`mem_vPairRFinset`).** A token lies in the mem v Pair Rfinite set exactly when a matching constructor in the set contributes it.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`vPairRFinset.empty`).** The empty of the empty set is empty.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Theorem (`vPairRFinset.insert_top`).** Inserting the indicated constructor updates insert top by adding that payload.

*Proof.* By cases on the constructors, or by the matching clause of consistency or entailment. □


**Definition (`VEnt`).** The vEnt are given by the listed constructors.


